    <description>A master of a craft, and the apprentice who followed them out to the edge of the world to learn it. The master has a lifetime of knowledge to pass on. The apprentice has the patience to learn it, most days.\n\nWord of a good workshop travels: in a week or two a travelling scholar will stop by, and later someone else may come wanting to learn, or an old friend of the master's may turn up. Nobody is waiting to attack you here. Just the work, and the slow satisfaction of getting better at it.</description>
